    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSpace, style and an abundance of natural light marry perfectly together in this exceptionally attractive, contemporary home in a peaceful private enclave. Occupying an impressive 145 sq m (approx.) and arranged over three well-proportioned floors, this beautifully presented modern home offers an exceptional combination of space, privacy and contemporary living. Built in 2019 by Colimore Homes, the property forms part of a discreet and tranquil enclave comprising just three apartments and eleven houses, creating a wonderfully private setting away from the hustle and bustle of the surrounding area.\nFrom the moment you enter, the abundance of natural light is immediately apparent. Large windows throughout the property, together with cleverly positioned roof lights, draw daylight deep into the home and create a bright and uplifting atmosphere across all three levels.\nThroughout the ground floor, beautiful engineered oiled white oak timber flooring (with under floor heating) adds warmth and continuity, complementing the property's clean, contemporary aesthetic. This level is particularly well suited to modern family living, with a welcoming reception room to the front featuring an attractive built-in media unit, while a generous guest WC adds further convenience. To the rear is the true heart of the home: a superb open-plan kitchen and dining space, finished in a contemporary style and centered around a substantial island unit. Full-height glazing provides a wonderful connection to the garden, while the south-facing rear garden enjoys excellent privacy, framed by mature trees. A useful utility area adjoins the kitchen and is conveniently plumbed for a washing machine.\nThe first floor provides two double bedrooms, both benefiting from fitted storage, with one enjoying the added luxury of a private en-suite. A stylish family bathroom completes this level, finished with smart marble-effect tiling. Continuing to the top floor, a strategically placed roof light above the stairwell floods the upper landing with natural light. Here, there is a further generous double bedroom with its own en suite, alongside a versatile attic room currently arranged as a study. This additional space offers considerable flexibility and could readily appeal to purchasers looking for a fourth bedroom, home office or additional living space. \nOutside, the secluded south-facing garden provides a peaceful private retreat, while the property's position within this small enclave gives a genuine sense of quiet and seclusion with off street parking to the front for two cars.\nWith its generous proportions, three-floor layout, wealth of natural light and flexible accommodation, this is a home that combines the practicality of modern family living with a distinctly private and tranquil setting. Its convenient location also provides easy access to local schools, shopping facilities and transport links, making it an ideal choice for those seeking both connectivity and calm."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance lobby: - 3.75m x 3.51m\nlightwell, engineered wood floors, recessed lighting, cloaks and shoe cubby\n\nLiving Room: - 4.24m x 3.91m\nengineered wood floor, floor to ceiling light bearing windows, recessed lighting, wall mounted media unit incorporating closed storage and display cabinetry\n\nGuest WC: - 1.50m x 1.46m\ntiled floor, tiled splashback, wall mounted WC, WHB, recessed lighting\n\nKitchen/Dining: - 5.26m x 4.75m\nengineered wood floor, light well, recessed lighting, island unit with electrical points, sink, dishwasher and granite countertop. There is wall to wall fitted kitchen units incorporating a Siemens oven, Siemens microwave, pull out larger, fridge / freezer and Siemens five ring induction hob, extractor fan flaked by granite countertops and splashback. A sliding floor into the garden is set into floor to ceiling gazing\n\nUtility Room: - 2.51m x 1.98m\nbuilt-in storage, plumbed for washing machine.\n\nFirst floor: - \n\n\nLanding: - \naccess to hot press, recess lighting.\n\nBedroom 2: - 3.88m x 3.28m\nexceptionally bright generous double bedroom with two floor sealing windows, laminate floor, built-in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom: - 2.10m x 2.04m\nmarble effect tiled floor and walls, WC with recessed cistern, w.h.b. wall mounted medicine cabinet, bath with shower, recess lighting.\n\nBedroom 1: - 3.90m x 3.22m\nlaminate floor, wall mounted shelving, two large light bearing floor ceiling window windows, built-in wardrobes.\n\nEn-suite: - 2.74m x 0.90m\nmarble effect tiled floor and part tiles tiled walls, step in shower cubicle with rainwater showerhead and secondary shower attachment, recessed lighting, w.h.b., w.c. with recessed cistern and heated towel royal\n\nTop floor - \n\n\nLanding: - 3.88m x 2.90m\na large Velux window allows light to flow down the stairwell and fill the landing with natural, there is a further window on the landing along with recessed lighting and Stira attic access.\n\nBedroom 3: - 3.88m x 3.31m\nlaminate floor, large light bearing window, built-in storage,\n\nEn-suite: - 2.62m x 0.90m\nmarble effect tiled floor, part tiles marble effect walls, recessed lighting, step in shower cubicle with rainwater showerhead and secondary shower attachment, w.c. with recessed cistern, w.h.b., heated towel rail.\n\nAttic Room: - 3.87m x 3.25m\nwith recessed lighting, Velux window, access to eaves storage, currently in use as a study\n\nGarden - \nTo the rear of the house a sliding door from the kitchen/dining opens onto a patio for outdoor relaxation, dining and entertainment. There is a large lawn area with a garden shed and mature trees at the end of the garden afford the garden a great degree of privacy. The garden is also provided with a green house\n\n"
